# Naming Convention

Security groups use SEC-<Type>-<Name>, for example
SEC-Dept-Sales or SEC-Role-Helpdesk. SEC identifies a
security group, Type describes its purpose, and Name
identifies the department or job function. Consistent
names make groups easier to find and understand.

User sign-in names use firstname.lastname followed by
@middenikhilvinaykumargmail.onmicrosoft.com.
All names use lowercase letters. This gives each fictional
person a predictable, individual account.
